  "description": "A bike after this writer's heart,\n\nthe Fuji Track is solid evidence that you can, after all, buy love.\n\nThe Track is a single-speed, no-coasting, totally simple bicycle - loved by\n\nbike messengers, winter trainers, real-rider cyclo-commuters and all those\n\nwho appreciate the elemental riding experience. And oh yeah, track racers.\n\nOn the road, fixed-gear pedaling keeps you warm in winter and smoothes the\n\nroughness a season's big-gear pounding leaves in your spin. It gives you control\n\nof your bike undreamed-of by derailleur bike riders. You feel geared to the\n\nroad. We fussed over the Track and we feel it's just what you\n\nwant. It has road geometry, it's drilled for front and rear brakes, the rear\n\nhub flip-flops so you can put a single-speed freewheel on one side if you\n\nwish (wuss) or two different fixed cogs on the opposite sides.\n\nThe Track harkens back to old-school Fujis and a few bikes from other enlightened\n\nmakers. If we have a clue who you are, and we think we do, we think the Track\n\nis the bike you'll still be in love with years from now.",
